// ────────────── Startup Applications ──────────────
// https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri/wiki/Configuration:-Miscellaneous#spawn-sh-at-startup

// Spawn processes at startup. Two variants:
//
//   spawn-at-startup "cmd" "arg1" "arg2"
//     Runs the command directly via execvp — fastest, no shell overhead.
//     Use this for apps that don't need shell features.
//
//   spawn-sh-at-startup "shell command here"
//     Runs via sh -c, so you can use pipes, redirection, env vars, etc.
//     Slightly slower due to shell startup.
//
// Note: running niri as a session supports xdg-desktop-autostart
// (~/.config/autostart/*.desktop), which may be more convenient for
// apps that already have desktop entries.

// All autostart entries live in cfg/autostart-machine.kdl (machine-specific).
// hotkey-overlay and screenshot-path are set in misc.kdl
